You certainly have a model of some concrete situation in mind; so let me
make a couple of more general remarks...

Wands of digging don't work on walls in Sokoban, they are also ineffective
if aimed at boulders. For the latter purpose use striking (force bolt) or
teleportation. (Destroying boulders will result in a luck penalty.)
Level two of Sokoban on your way back is not very specific WRT a bunch of
blocking boulders in a corridor; superfluous boulders will typically be a
problem everywhere in Sokoban, specifically in corridors.
Path blocking boulders can be passed if not carrying much; you are at least
not trapped and can get new equipment from your stashes before you come back
to get what you left back. (Squeezing past boulders will also result in a
luck penalty.)
If you want to leave back something for weight considerations, do that on
the up-stairs to the next level; you can always be there first (if you don't
do something completely wrong), and items on other levels are safe while you
are on another level.
Generally avoid leaving items on the floor that monsters might use to their
advantage or to your harm; if you need to, always engrave the magic word on
that square.
Avoid combat with monsters if you know they possibly have picked up those
scrolls.
Always take something with you as an option to escape (even with a penalty),
like a pick-axe, wands of teleportation, striking, means to polymorph self,
etc.

